  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Two matched local swap histories create a physical ordinary order record, with a physical two-time control. They do not generate or detect opposite relative signs on the same complete word pair. For a common retained-record kernel the output difference is bounded by retained total variation. For normalized affine two-word effects the precise contrast is twice the real off-diagonal coefficient. Deterministic singleton event calibration, diagonal-pullback histories and complete nonnegative instruments imply zero contrast. Perfect sign contrast forces both singleton chances one half.",
